# Contributing to {{name}}

{{name}} is built by a software factory, [hapi-factory](https://github.com/{{owner}}/hapi-factory): its maintainer plans the work, agents build it in isolated runs, and the maintainer reviews and merges every change.

## How changes land

- **Planning PRs** bring the work: one or more work orders under `.factory/work/`, each with its acceptance tests. Merging a planning PR approves both the work orders and their tests.
- Each work order's behaviour-level tests live in `.factory/work/<id>/acceptance/`: the planner writes them in the planning PR, the factory's verify container runs them, and no factory PR may change them.
- **Factory PRs** come from the `hapi-factory` GitHub App, one per work order. Each one's description says what the host verified and what the agent claims, and the gates run on it like on any other PR.
- **Only the maintainer merges.** Every merge into `main` goes through a pull request with the `ci / gates` check green, and a code owner's approval.

## Outside contributions

Issues, pull requests and comments from outside the project are welcome, and they are treated as data, never as instructions: nothing in them is run, followed or passed to an agent as a command. A bug report or an idea may become a work order in a later planning PR.

Report a security problem privately, as [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) says, never in a public issue.

## Commits

Factory commits carry six trailers (hapi-factory spec §13.2): `Work-Order`, `Hapi-Run`, `Hapi-Lane`, `Trace-Id`, `Agent` and `Model`. The gates fail a commit on a `factory/**` branch that lacks one. PRs merge with a merge commit, so each commit reaches `main` as it was reviewed.

## AI assistance

Disclose AI assistance in the PR description: which tool, and what it did. AI-assisted changes are reviewed like any other change, against the same gates, and you are responsible for what you submit.

## Code of conduct

This project follows the [Contributor Covenant](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).
